#[doc("""
Text the source wrote, kept apart from the identity it resolves to.

A name is not an identity. The resolver turns what the source wrote into
a `SymId`, and every pass after it decides by that id. The characters
survive for three readers only: the resolver, which has nothing else to
look up; a diagnostic, which shows them; and an emitter, which spells a
symbol from them.

`Written` makes that boundary a type. Its one field is private, so the
characters leave only through `written_text`, and a diagnostic
interpolates the value directly. Nothing here answers whether two
written names are the same declaration: that question has an id.
""")]

#[doc("A name as the source spelled it.")]
#[derive(BinSerialize)]
pub type Written = { priv text: String }

#[doc("The written form of `s`.")]
pub fn written(s: String) : Written = Written { text: s }

#[doc("The characters of `w`, for the resolver's lookups and an emitter's spelling.")]
pub fn written_text(w: Written) : String = w.text

impl Show for Written {
  fn show(w: Written) : String = w.text
}
